            <ArticleTitle>Survey on etiological diagnosis of diabetes in 1244 Italian diabetic children and adolescents: impact of access to genetic testing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e15-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2015.01.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0168-8227(15)00011-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Type 2 and monogenic diabetes are emerging causes of diabetes in youths. Among 1244 Italian patients &lt;18 years of age, 91.9% had type 1, 0.2% type 2, and 4.9% monogenic diabetes. Monogenic diabetes ranks second as a cause of diabetes in Italian youth, while type 2 diabetes appears to be rare.</AbstractText>
